Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect argument being passed to the `advance` method, using `valuesDocID` instead of the current document `doc`. This resulted in improper advancement of document values, leading to inaccurate outcome collection during query processing in the logistic regression parser.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
int valuesDocID = leafOutcomeValue.docID();
valuesDocID = leafOutcomeValue.advance(valuesDocID);
```
Reason:
The method `advance` was incorrectly called with `valuesDocID`, which is the ID of the last document processed, instead of the current document `doc`. This caused the advancement logic to be based on an outdated document ID, resulting in improper collection of outcome values during query processing.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
valuesDocID = leafOutcomeValue.advance(doc);
```
Reason:
By changing the argument of the `advance` method to the current document `doc`, the advancement of document values is now aligned with the current processing context, ensuring accurate collection of outcome values. This fix addresses the root cause of the bug by correctly passing the intended document ID for advancement.


